1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,960
Okay, Chandler, Mon, there's only one banana nut muffin left.
好啦，錢德勒、摩妮卡，只剩下一個香蕉核桃馬芬了。

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,280
Well, order mine first.
那就先點我的。

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,340
Yeah, but I'm so much faster.
是啊，但我動作快得多。

5
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,900
Give it to me.
給我。

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,080
No.
不。

7
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,880
Give it to me.
給我吧。

8
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,240
Okay, you can have it.
好吧，給你。

9
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,200
There you go. Enjoy your coffee.
這個給你。好好享用你的咖啡。

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,600
That was there when I got here.
我剛來的時候那就在這了。

11
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:36,320
Hey, you guys, you will never guess who's coming to New York.
嘿，各位，你們絕對猜不到誰要來紐約了。

12
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,580
Wait, Phoebe, tell us before you can swallow.
等等，菲比，嚥下東西前先告訴我們。

13
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,960
Okay, Ryan, that guy I went out with who's in the Navy.
好吧，是瑞恩，那個和我約會過、在海軍服役的傢伙。

14
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,420
You went out with a guy in the Navy?
你跟海軍約會過？

15
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:47,980
Yeah, I met him when I was playing guitar in Washington Square Park.
對啊，我在華盛頓廣場公園彈吉他時認識他的。

16
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:50,720
Ryan threw in saltwater taffy because he didn't have any change.
瑞恩丟了鹹水太妃糖給我，因為他沒零錢。

17
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,720
Hey, is that when you rode saltwater taffy, man?
嘿，老兄，那就是你創作「鹹水太妃糖」這首歌的時候嗎？

18
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:54,540
No.
不是。

19
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:58,580
No, he is my submarine guy.
不，他是我的潛水艇男孩。

20
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,680
He resurfaces, like, every couple years,
他大概每幾年才會浮出水面一次，

21
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,580
and we have the most amazing three days together.
然後我們會一起度過最不可思議的三天。

22
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,520
Only this time, he's coming for two weeks.
不過這次，他會待上整整兩個星期。

23
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:07,700
Two whole weeks, which means, yay!
整整兩個星期，意思是說，耶！

24
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:13,100
So, wait, this guy goes down for, like, two years at a time?
所以，等等，這傢伙一次潛下去就是在下面待個兩年？

25
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:13,740
Mm-mm.
嗯哼。

26
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:18,160
That'll teach you to lick my muffin.
這就是你舔我馬芬的下場。

27
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:19,560
Hi.
嗨。

28
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:23,980
Hi.
嗨。

29
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:26,720
Oh, no, what happened?
噢不能，發生什麼事了？

30
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,540
I just spoke to Carol. Ben's got the chicken pox.
我剛跟卡蘿通完電話。班得了水痘。

31
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:30,840
Oh, are you kidding?
噢，你開玩笑吧？

32
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:34,140
Yeah, so if you haven't already had it, chances are you're gonna get it.
對，所以如果你們還沒得過，很有可能會被傳染。

33
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,240
Well, I've had it.
嗯，我得過了。

34
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,160
Yeah, I've had it.
對，我得過了。

35
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:36,760
Had it.
得過了。

36
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:37,280
Had it.
得過了。

37
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:39,460
Well, I haven't ever had it. I feel so left out.
嗯，我從來沒得過。覺得自己好被排擠喔。

38
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,100
Oh, look!
哦，看！

39
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:54,000
So no one told you life was gonna be this way
所以沒人告訴過你生活會是這樣

40
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,780
Your job's a joke, you're broke
工作是個笑話，你身無分文

41
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:59,520
Your love life's the only way
你的感情生活就是這樣

42
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:03,480
It's like you're always stuck in second gear
就像你總是被卡在二檔

43
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:07,700
When it hasn't been your day, week, or month
當這不是屬於你的一天、一週或一個月

44
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:09,240
Or even your year
甚至不是屬於你的一年

45
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:12,640
But I'll be there for you
但我會在你身邊

46
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:15,000
When the rain starts to pour
當大雨傾盆時

47
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,560
I'll be there for you
我會在你身邊

48
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,040
I'll be there for you
我會在你身邊

49
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,580
I'll be there for you
我會在你身邊

50
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,160
I'll be there for you too
我也會在你身邊

51
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,840
Honey, you made the bed again.
親愛的，你又重新鋪了一次床。

52
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:39,240
I told you, you don't have to do that.
我跟你說過你不用這樣做。

53
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,440
This isn't camp.
這裡又不是夏令營。

54
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:44,440
Oh, then I guess the panty raid last night was totally uncalled for.
噢，那我猜昨晚去女生宿舍偷內褲的行動完全是多此一舉了囉。

55
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:47,600
Okay, I am going to take a shower,
好了，我要去洗澡了，

56
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:51,020
and today I will be singing Jim Croce's Leroy Brown.
而且今天我要高唱 Jim Croce 的 Leroy Brown。

57
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,000
Monica!
摩妮卡！

58
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:03,660
Hey, Mon.
嘿，小摩。

59
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,040
I have a question.
我有一個問題。

60
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,040
Is Leroy the baddest man in the whole damn town
Leroy 是全鎮「最壞的男人」

61
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,040
or the fattest man in the whole damn town?
還是全鎮「最胖的男人」？

62
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:12,880
The baddest.
最壞的男人。

63
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:15,700
Otherwise, the song would be Fat, Fat Leroy Brown.
不然這首歌就會變成胖子、胖子 Leroy Brown 了。

64
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,680
What are you doing?
你在做什麼？

65
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,780
I'm just waiting for you, sweetie.
我只是在等你啊，親愛的。

66
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,220
Are you remaking the bed?
你在重新鋪床嗎？

67
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,120
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
對不起。對不起。

68
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,180
You know what? The way you did it, it was just fine.
你知道嗎？你剛剛鋪的樣子其實很不錯。

69
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,740
Then you're redoing it because?
那你還要重鋪是因為？

70
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,720
If I tell you, you'll think I'm crazy.
如果我告訴你，你會覺得我瘋了。

71
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,080
You're pretty much running that risk either way.
不管怎樣你都已經冒著讓我這麼覺得的風險了。

72
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:41,680
Okay, you see,
好，你看，

73
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:47,120
the duvet tag shouldn't be at the top left corner.
羽絨被的標籤不該在左上角。

74
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,080
It should be at the bottom right corner.
它應該在右下角。

75
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:50,940
Oh, well, that's not so crazy.
噢，那也沒那麼瘋狂拉。

76
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,420
I'm just easing you in.
我這只是個開場白。

77
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:53,780
All right.
好吧。

78
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:56,660
All right, you see these little flower blossoms?
好，你看到這些小花苞嗎？

79
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,580
They should be facing up, not down,
它們的頭應該要朝上，不是朝下，

80
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,420
because, well, the head of the bed is where the sun would be.
因為床頭就是太陽的方向。

81
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,060
You don't love me anymore.
你不再愛我了。

82
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,900
Actually, if it's possible, I love you more.
事實上，如果可以的話，我反而更愛你。

83
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:15,420
Really?
真的嗎？

84
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,960
Wow. Well, then, come on.
哇喔。那麼，過來吧。

85
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:22,660
I want to show you how to fold a toilet paper into a point.
我想給你看看怎麼把衛生紙摺成一個尖角。

86
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,140
Hey, look, Joey, I'm just saying,
嘿，聽著，喬伊，我只是覺得，

87
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,160
if you need something to hold you over,
如果你需要一份可以撐一下的工作，

88
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,760
I can get you a job right here as an entry-level processor.
我可以幫你在這裡找一份初級資料處理員的職缺。

89
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:35,120
But don't you need experience for a job like that?
但做這個不用經驗嗎？

90
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,500
It's not that hard to learn.
這沒那麼難學。

91
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:39,340
And as for people realizing that you have no idea what you're doing,
至於要是大家發現你根本不知道自己在幹嘛這點嘛，

92
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:42,000
hey, you're an actor. Act like a processor.
嘿，你可是演員。就演成一個資料處理員啊。

93
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,060
People will think you're a processor.
那大家就會以為你是一個真正的資料處理員了。

94
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:47,860
Hey, Chandler, here's this morning's projection.
嘿，錢德勒，這是今天早上的預測報表。

95
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:49,920
Hey, thanks. Scott Alexander, Joey Tribbiani.
嘿，謝啦。史考特·亞歷山大，這位是喬伊·崔比雅尼。

96
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:50,660
Hey.
嘿。

97
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,800
Joey is a, uh, fellow processor.
喬伊他，呃，也是我們資料處理的同事。

98
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,220
No kidding.
不開玩笑吧。

99
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,340
Oh, yeah, yeah.
噢對，沒錯。

100
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,540
I process. People want the processing. 
我是處理員。大家想要處理資料。

101
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,380
I'm the one they call.
他們就會找我。

102
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,420
Where do you work?
你在哪高就？

103
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:08,160
Uh, well, right now I'm in between things.
嗯，我現在是在空窗期啦。

104
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,220
You know how it is. One day you're processing,
你知道這行嘛，可能今天還有料要處理，

105
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:14,260
the next day you're not so much processing anymore.
明天就沒什麼好處理了。

106
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:17,140
I was just telling Joey about the opening in Fleischman's Group.
我剛剛正告訴喬伊關於弗雷希曼小組的職缺。

107
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:18,400
Fleischman's Group?
弗雷希曼小組？

108
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,500
Whatever you do, don't touch his sandwiches.
不管你遇到誰，千萬不要碰他的三明治。

109
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,080
Are all you processors dorks?
你們做資料處理的都這麼怪胎阿？

110
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,800
Ugh. This lipstick looks just great on you.
呃，這支口紅塗在你嘴上真好看。

111
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,440
You look fabulous, honey. You really do.
你美極了，親愛的，真的。

112
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:40,780
Yeah? Are you sure? Really?
是嗎？確定？真的？

113
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:46,520
See? You look beautiful. For God's sakes, dim the lights.
看？你很美啊。看在老天的份上，把燈調暗點。

114
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,140
Are you... I...
你是...我...

115
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,820
I'm hideous.
我醜死了。

116
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,200
It's gonna be okay.
一切都會沒事的。

117
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,060
Ryan's been underwater.
瑞恩都在海裡面待那麼久了。

118
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:57,060
He's just gonna be so glad that you don't have barbs anymore.
光想到你身上沒有長滿海藻，他就該偷笑了。

119
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,500
Come in.
請進。

120
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,280
Hey, baby, I'm back.
嘿，寶貝，我回來了。

121
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,140
Hey, Ryan, what's up?
嘿，瑞恩，怎麼啦？

122
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,420
What's going on?
怎麼了？

123
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,160
Oh, no, no. You know, you have to stay back.
噢，不...不行。你得離我遠點。

124
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,120
I... I have the pox.
我...我長水痘了。

125
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:27,940
Hey.
嘿。

126
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,120
Chicken or small?
水痘 (chicken pox) 還是天花 (smallpox)？

127
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,020
Chicken, which is so ironic,
是水痘 (chicken)，滿諷刺的，

128
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,340
considering I'm a vegetarian.
畢竟我是個吃純素的人。

129
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:36,580
Why aren't you at home in bed?
你為什麼不躺在家的床上？

130
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,220
Because my grandmother's never had chicken pox.
因為我外婆從沒得過水痘。

131
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:41,840
Please, please tell me you have,
拜託，求你告訴我你得過了，

132
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,020
because, oh, my God, I forgot how cute you are.
因為，我的老天，我都忘了你有多可愛了。

133
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,140
I'm sorry. I never had them.
抱歉，我從沒得過。

134
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,620
If I had one wish,
如果我可以許一個願，

135
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,260
it would be to build a time machine, go back to when I was seven.
那就是建造一台時光機，回到七歲的時候。

136
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,560
When Jimmy Houser had the chicken pox,
當吉米·豪瑟得水痘的時後，

137
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,960
I would grab that kid and rub him all over my face.
我一定要抓住那孩子，把他的臉到處亂揉。

138
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,080
Yeah, or, you know,
是啊，或著，你知道的，

139
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:00,800
you could just wish that I didn't have them now.
你也可以祈禱我現在身上沒長這些。

140
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:03,360
Can I please see your face?
我能看看你的臉嗎？

141
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:03,800
No.
不行。

142
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,380
You don't want to see your face covered with pox.
你不會想看到一張長滿水痘的臉的。

143
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,520
Your face could be covered with locks. I wouldn't care.
哪怕你的臉上都是密碼鎖，我也不在乎。

144
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,520
And you hate fish.
而你討厭魚(或者海草)。

145
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:11,960
Oh.
噢。

146
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,840
So sweet.
好甜。

147
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:16,460
All right. Okay.
好吧，歐給。

148
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,740
All right, you can see.
好啦，你看吧。

149
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:21,000
This is me.
這就是我。

150
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,420
Oh, sorry.
噢抱歉。

151
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,060
Oh, I am scary.
噢，這真的很可怕。

152
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:29,880
Sorry, the lightning.
抱歉，這是閃電 (被閃電嚇到)。

153
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:32,100
Lightning was an unfortunate coincidence.
剛好有閃電真是個不幸的巧合。

154
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:34,580
You look lovely.
你看起來很美麗。

155
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:35,520
Lovely.
美麗極了。

156
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,300
I hate this.
我討厭這樣。

157
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:41,000
Can I tell you, I had the most amazing two weeks planned for us,
這我一定要跟你說，我本來為我們計畫了最棒的兩週，

158
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,840
and almost everything I had in mind,
而在我想像中的每一件事裡，

159
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,520
we had to be a lot closer than this.
我們的距離都得比現在這樣近得多。

160
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:48,340
Phoebe, I have spent the last eight months
菲比，過去這八個月裡，

161
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,920
in a steel tube with men.
我都和一群男人擠在鐵管裡面。

162
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:53,300
Thinking about this moment,
想著這一刻的回來到來，

163
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,880
I am not going to let a bunch of
我絕對不會讓這些

164
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:58,740
itchy spots
發癢的小疹子

165
00:07:58,740 --> 00:07:59,680
stand between us.
阻礙我們。

166
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,520
Okay, this is the most romantic disease I've ever had.
好吧，這可真是我得過最浪漫的病了。

167
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:16,840
Hey.
嘿。

168
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,480
Hey, how's the first week going?
嘿，第一週過得怎麼樣啊？

169
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,180
Pretty good. It's like you said.
很順利。就如你所說，

170
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,220
It's mostly just putting numbers from one column
就只是把其中一欄的數字

171
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,360
into another column.
搬到另一欄去而已。
172
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,300
Well, there you go.
嗯，那不就結了。

173
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,360
Hey, and everybody is so nice.
嘿，而且大家都超好的。

174
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,180
I just had a good talk with that lady with the red hair, Jeannie.
我剛才還和那個紅頭髮女士 Jeannie 相處得滿愉快的。

175
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,160
Jeannie? The head of East Coast Operations, Jeannie?
Jeannie？東岸營運主管 Jeannie？

176
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:32,700
Yeah.
對阿。

177
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,980
Turns out our kids go to the same school.
我們剛好聊到我們的小孩上同一間學校。

178
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,300
Yeah.
阿哈。

179
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,420
Small world, huh?
世界真小，對吧？

180
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:42,780
Weird world.
這世界真怪。

181
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:45,220
Your kids?
你的小孩？

182
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:47,360
I figure my character has kids.
我覺得我這個角色應該要有小孩才合理。

183
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,780
You know, there isn't a part of that sentence
你知道，其實剛才你說的那句話裡，沒有一個部分，

184
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:52,660
that I don't need explained?
是不需要解釋給我聽的。

185
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,280
Well, see, when you're acting,
嗯，你看，演戲的時候嘛，

186
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,960
you need to think about stuff like that.
你就是得設定好這些細節。

187
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:59,560
My character, Joseph the Processing Guy,
我演的角色，Joseph，身為一個資料處理員，

188
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,840
has two little girls,
有兩個小女兒，

189
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:03,060
Ashley and Brittany.
Ashley 和 Brittany。

190
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:07,720
Ashley copies everything Brittany does.
Ashley 做什麼事都學 Brittany。

191
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:12,640
Oh.
噢。

192
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:16,240
Well, invisible kids can be that way sometimes.
嗯，有時候看不見的小孩就是這樣。

193
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:19,880
You know, Joseph and his wife, Karen,
你知道嗎，Joseph 和他太太 Karen，

194
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:21,560
are thinking of having a third kid.
正在考慮要生第三個小孩。

195
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:23,620
You know what?
你猜怎麼著？

196
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,680
Just did.
有了。

197
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,360
Really? Wow.
真的？哇喔。

198
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:31,500
That's some pretty powerful imaginary sperm you must have there.
看來你的幻想精子滿有威力的嘛。

199
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,280
You know what makes the itching even worse?
你知道有什麼東西會讓你更癢嗎？

200
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,940
That you don't stop talking about it?
你這張停不下來抱怨的嘴嗎？

201
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,040
Fine.
好吧。

202
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:51,560
Let's just play, okay?
我們繼續玩吧，好嗎？

203
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:53,360
Good. Okay.
很好。

204
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,380
Here we go. Double sixes.
來了。兩個六。

205
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,040
Here we go.
換我。

206
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,660
Here we go.
換我了。

207
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:01,480
Come to mama.
骰子乖，過來媽媽這。

208
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,740
Getting ready to roll the dice.
準備扔骰子了。

209
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:05,480
What are you doing?
你在幹什麼？

210
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:06,920
Are you scratching?
你在抓癢對吧？

211
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,720
No. This is what I do for luck, okay?
才沒有。這不過是能幫我祈求好運的動作罷了，好嗎？

212
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:11,920
You're scratching.
你真的在抓！

213
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:13,720
Give me the dice. No.
骰子給我。不給。

214
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,600
Give me the dice.
給我。

215
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,840
Here, there. Double sixes.
來了。兩個六。

216
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,760
We can't scratch. You know we can't.
我們不能抓的。你知道的。

217
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,260
We'll scar.
我們身上會留疤的。

218
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:25,420
I can't stop thinking about it.
我滿腦子都是很想抓的念頭。

219
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,540
It's so hard.
這真的太難了。

220
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:30,140
I just want to grab all these houses and rub them all over my body.
我只想拿起這些（大富翁的）小房子，把它們全搓在我身上。

221
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:30,620
No.
不行。

222
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:33,100
Come on.
求你啦。

223
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,580
You know you want it.
我知道你也想抓的。

224
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,240
You know you want it too. Come on.
你也一定很想阿，來嘛。

225
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,360
Let's just be bad. It'll feel so good.
我們就做壞事吧。肯定超舒服。

226
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:39,600
Come on.
別忍了。

227
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,560
Uh-huh.
嗯。

228
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:42,780
God help me.
上帝幫幫我。

229
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:44,760
Yeah.
呼。

230
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,580
Okay, good. Now do me.
好，很好。現在換幫我弄。

231
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,000
Do my back. Come on. Harder.
幫我抓背。快點。再大力點。

232
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,300
There you go. Don't move.
很好喔。別停！

233
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:52,940
Why?
為什麼？

234
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:54,460
Oh.
噢。

235
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:56,360
Okay.
好。

236
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,020
Stop that.
停下來。

237
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,200
Stop that right now.
快點停下來。

238
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:04,120
You know, I might have expected this of you, Phoebe,
菲比，我可能早就料到你會有這反應，

239
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:06,260
but Ryan, you're a military man.
但瑞恩，你可是一名軍人。

240
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,000
She made me do it.
是她逼我的。

241
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,900
Oh, that's a nice color on you.
哦，那顏色真配你。

242
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:15,200
Yeah, well, it comes in pink and blotchy, baby.
這就是粉紅又起疹的顏色，寶貝。

243
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,520
I hope you get a weenie pock.
我希望你的GG上也長一顆水痘。

244
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:25,160
You and Milton have to join us on the boat.
你和彌爾頓這次必須和我們一起搭船去。

245
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:26,840
Karen will pack a lunch.
凱倫可以帶你們去吃午餐。

246
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,540
You'll bring the kids. We'll make a day of it.
你們帶著你們的小孩，我們會度過充實的一天。

247
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:29,720
Oh, that sounds lovely.
聽起來真棒。

248
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:31,360
We're going to have to set that up.
我們一定要約個時間。

249
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,800
Oh, I better get back.
噢，我該回去了。

250
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,360
Hope the baby feels better.
希望小寶寶能好點。

251
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,920
Oh, thanks. Thanks.
噢，謝謝。謝謝啦。

252
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,080
Bye-bye, Jeannie.
拜拜。珍妮。

253
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:39,960
What a phony.
真是什麼騙子都有。

254
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:45,000
Well, I'm sure you'll teach her a lesson
好吧，我相信總有一天你會讓她記取教訓的，

255
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,160
when she steps off the dock onto nothing.
比如當她從港口走下來什麼都沒有發現的時候。

256
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,300
Hey, Mr. Douglas. Sir?
嘿，道格拉斯先生，對嗎？

257
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:52,300
Uh, listen, Bing, I received your memo,
呃，聽著，賓先生，我收到你的備忘錄了，

258
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,200
so we're not going to see the systems report until next Friday?
所以我們要到下週五才會看到系統報告是嗎？

259
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,720
Well, the people in my group want to spend
因為我們這一組的人想利用這個連續假日，

260
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,040
the holiday weekend with their family.
多一點時間陪家人。

261
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:00,240
I have a family. I'm going to be here.
我也有家人啊，但我還是會在這邊。

262
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:01,800
Yeah, Bing.
是吧，賓先生。

263
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:03,360
What's that about?
那是怎麼一回事？

264
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,440
I want to give people a little slack,
我想讓大家放鬆一點，

265
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:11,580
you know, for morale.
你知道，這樣對士氣有幫助。

266
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,320
Look, if you want to see some rough numbers,
聽好，如果您只是想看一些大概數字的話，

267
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,520
I can get them to you by Wednesday.
我禮拜三前可以給你。

268
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,060
Rough numbers?
大概數字？

269
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,800
This company was not built on rough numbers.
這家公司可不是建立在「大概的數字」上的。

270
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:21,260
Am I right, Mr. Douglas?
我說得對吧，道格拉斯先生？

271
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:24,920
Have the final numbers on my desk by Tuesday.
請在星期二的時候，把最後的數字放在我桌上。

272
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,720
If you say so, sir.
如果您堅持的話，長官。

273
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,700
Joseph's good, isn't he?
這個約瑟夫表現不錯，對吧？

274
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,940
Well, I'm going to kill you.
是阿，我絕對要宰了你。

275
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,260
Hey, hey.
嘿，聽著。

276
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,660
I just figured Joseph's the kind of guy
我想這個約瑟夫應該也是個這方面的人才，

277
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:39,680
who likes to mix it up.
很喜歡攪和這些事。

278
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:42,240
You know, get in there, ruffle some feathers.
你懂得，深入敵營，故意去惹毛誰的。

279
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,000
Why?
為什麼他要這樣？

280
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,560
Look, I'm sorry,
這點我真的很抱歉，

281
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,120
but that's what Joseph does.
不過這就是約瑟夫會做的事。

282
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:51,900
Okay?
了解嗎？

283
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,460
If you try to pull something,
若是你想搞些什麼小花招，

284
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,000
he'll call you on it.
他一定會直接點出來。

285
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,100
What are you trying to pull, he'll say.
像是「你想耍什麼花招」，他就會這樣問。

286
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:04,760
Ooh, duct tape.
喔，是防水布膠帶。

287
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,060
Was I supposed to bring something, too?
所以我也還需要繼續拿別的東西來嗎？

288
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,520
This is for the scratchy twins out there.
我是要給外面那些快被抓癢逼瘋的雙胞胎用的。

289
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,960
I taped oven mitts to their hands.
我用膠帶把烤箱手套黏在他們手上。

290
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,840
You're strict.
你真嚴格。

291
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,820
Yeah, well, it's for their own good.
這可是為了他們好。

292
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:18,780
You know, I like
你懂我為甚麼喜歡

293
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,400
the way you have efficiently
你這麼俐落乾脆地

294
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,960
folded this tab under.
就把這些膠帶捲到底下的樣子嗎。

295
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:23,880
See, in a tape emergency,
你看，要是在這個有關膠帶的緊急狀況時，

296
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:26,440
you could shave valuable seconds off your time.
你就可以幫我們爭取幾秒鐘寶貴的時間了。

297
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:28,900
Exactly.
一點也沒錯。

298
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:29,720
Oh.
噢。

299
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,800
I love that I can be totally neurotic
我真的很喜歡、在現在這情況中

300
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:33,540
around you now.
完完全全為了你瘋狂。

301
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:35,960
Tell me the truth.
老實跟我說吧。

302
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:38,820
Don't you like it better now that everything on your desk
你現在難道沒有比以前那桌上

303
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,380
is perpendicular?
東西全擺在一起的情況喜歡這一切嗎？

304
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:43,020
If it's not a right angle, it is a wrong angle.
如果它看起來是不對（right）的角度，那它就是一個錯的（wrong）角度。

305
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:44,720
Very good.
講的不錯喔。

306
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:45,320
Thank you.
感謝。

307
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:48,040
You know what? Tomorrow, I'm going to do your clocks.
你猜怎麼著？明天，我要把你的那些老鐘給辦了。

308
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,660
You're going to do what to my clocks?
你到底要對我的那些鐘做了什麼？

309
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,400
I'm going to set them to my time.
我要把它們調成跟我一樣的時區。

310
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,200
Well, I'm confused.
這可真把我搞糊塗了。

311
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,480
I thought we shared time.
我以為我們是活在同一的時間點。

312
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,540
No, no.
沒有、才沒呢。

313
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,060
See, in my bedroom,
你懂嗎？在我的房間裡，

314
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,840
I set my clocks six minutes fast.
我把時鐘調快了六分鐘。

315
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:04,800
You want to know why?
我想知道為什麼嗎？

316
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:08,520
Because it's in a slightly different time zone than the kitchen?
因為它剛好在這邊這個有那麼一點的時差的廚房裡？

317
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:10,680
You know what? Forget it.
你才怎麼著？算了。

318
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:11,200
I'm not going to tell you.
我才不想跟你說呢。

319
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,660
No, come on. Come on. Tell me.
別這樣嘛。別這樣啊，告訴我好不好？

320
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,120
No, because you don't understand.
不要，因為你根本不懂。

321
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:14,520
No, come on.
才不會，拜託告訴我嘛。

322
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,000
You don't have any of these cute little obsessive things.
因為妳全身上下一點這可愛且瘋狂的固執點都沒有。

323
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:17,860
No, that's not true.
胡說，哪有這種事。

324
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:18,800
That is not true.
這絕對不是真的。

325
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,420
Oh, yeah?
真的嗎？

326
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:19,960
Yeah.
對啊。

327
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:21,180
All right, well, tell me one of yours.
太好了，拿你就跟我說一個你的。

328
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:22,520
Okay.
好喔。

329
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:27,420
Ah!
啊哈！

330
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:29,520
One of my things is
其中一個就是──

331
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,820
I always separate
我總是會將我的毛巾襪

332
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:34,620
my sweat socks from my dress socks.
和一般的襪子全部分開來。

333
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,100
Yeah.
對。

334
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:39,280
What if they get mixed up?
那如果搞混了呢？

335
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:42,840
Boy, I would just, uh...
天啊，我這人大概就會直接、呃...

336
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,260
I would freak out.
我真的會崩潰。

337
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,460
You would not.
你才不會崩潰。

338
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,540
Oh, I can't believe this.
天啊這真的教我沒法相信。

339
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,260
I hate this. You're too normal.
我討厭這樣。我看你真的很不正常喔。

340
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:53,700
I can't believe my boyfriend doesn't have a thing.
我簡直無法去相信我的男朋友竟然沒有問題！
341
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,700
